      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Low-frequency, pulsed sounds around 17-19 Hz can sometimes be associated with infrasound, which is below the typical range of human hearing. In an urban environment, such regular, strong pulses could potentially be caused by large-scale machinery, structural resonance, or specialized low-frequency emitters. Given the consistency you've observed, investigating the building's subsurface infrastructure or nearby industrial power sources might reveal the source.",
